#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:1
msgid "Testing and CI"
msgstr "测试与 CI"

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:3
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:5
msgid "The suite lives in `tests/` and has three layers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:7
msgid "`tests/unit/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:8
msgid ""
"Catch2 unit tests for the shared library. They link `cneta_core` directly"
" and cover the state encoding, the rate and transition matrices, and the "
"tree helpers. Built only with `-DCNETA_BUILD_TESTING=ON`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:12
msgid "`tests/e2e/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:13
msgid ""
"pytest tests that run the compiled programs on a small simulated dataset,"
" checking output files, error handling, and reproducibility. Includes "
"smoke tests that execute the `run-*.sh` scripts as a user would."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:17
msgid "`tests/build_system/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:18
msgid ""
"pytest tests that configure and compile the project from scratch and "
"check `build.sh`'s argument handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:21
msgid ""
"To run everything, from the top of the repository with the `cneta-build` "
"environment active (it includes pytest; see "
"[Installation](../installation/index.md)):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:34
msgid ""
"Without conda, install pytest with `pip install -r "
"tests/requirements.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:36
msgid ""
"`OMP_NUM_THREADS=1` keeps timings comparable and a failure easy to repeat"
" by hand. `cnetml` parallelises its tree search with OpenMP, but the "
"result does not depend on the thread count; `test_cnetml.py` checks that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:40
msgid ""
"The regression anchor is `cnetml --mode 2`, which scores a supplied tree "
"with no RNG and no search and so is reproducible to the digit. Reference "
"values live in `tests/data/expected.json`. A change there means the "
"likelihood calculation changed — which is exactly what needs watching "
"during the `libcneta` refactor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:46
msgid ""
"[Writing a unit test](writing-tests.md) is the walkthrough for adding one"
" of your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:49
msgid ""
"`tests/README.md` has the full detail, including what is *not* covered "
"yet and a list of known failures the suite records but does not fail on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:52
msgid "Continuous integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:54
msgid "Workflows live in `.github/workflows/`. Currently:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:56
msgid "`docs.yml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:57
msgid ""
"builds the documentation on every pull request into `main`, and publishes"
" to GitHub Pages when a pull request is merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:60
msgid "`ci.yml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:61
msgid ""
"builds the project and runs the unit and end-to-end tests on `ubuntu-"
"latest` and `macos-latest`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/testing.md:64
msgid ""
"Both run on pull requests into `main` and on pushes to `main` — not on "
"every pushed commit, so work-in-progress on a branch with no open pull "
"request costs nothing. Both can also be triggered by hand from the "
"Actions tab (`workflow_dispatch`)."
msgstr ""

